{"id":844,"date":"2020-11-10T12:13:00","date_gmt":"2020-11-10T20:13:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=844"},"modified":"2024-09-01T15:59:45","modified_gmt":"2024-09-01T22:59:45","slug":"codrone-arduino-build-the-remote","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-arduino-build-the-remote\/","title":{"rendered":"Building the Remote"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215974e66b\" name=\"6a2215974e66b\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build video<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>If you&#8217;d like to see the full-length build video with more detail, you can check that out\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/youtu.be\/HAXq1gBO3I8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-link-type=\"LINK\">here<\/a>.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=mDDdWtQXyF4&amp;feature=emb_logo&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215974e783\" name=\"6a2215974e783\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>The Remote and the Control<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]1.Use two long bolts and two nuts to attach the blueboard to the Smart Inventor Board.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;845&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]2. Attach two short standoffs to the blueboard. They should be in the third and fifth columns in the third row.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;846&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]3. Attach the joysticks to their boards. They might have come already attached in your kit so if this is the case for you, skip this step![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;848&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215974e7da\" name=\"6a2215974e7da\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>2 Remote 2 Control<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]4. Bolt the joysticks to either side of the blueboards. The pins should be facing the Smart Inventor Board.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;847&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]5. Take the lid off the battery box. Bolt two short standoffs to the battery box. The standoffs should be on the outside![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;849&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]6. Attach the battery box to the bottom of the remote. The standoffs from the battery box should be in the fourth column and in the fourth and sixth rows.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;850&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]7. Next, bolt the Bluetooth board to the two standoffs on the blueboard.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;851&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215974e82a\" name=\"6a2215974e82a\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Remote Control: San Diego Drift<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]8. Plug the wire from the battery box into its place on the Smart Inventor Board.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;852&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]9. Plug the SVG connectors to the joystick pins and into the SVG ports on the Smart Inventor Board. Pay attention to the sequence of the colors and the orientation![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;853&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]10. Plug the black serial connector into its spot on the bottom lefthand corner of the Bluetooth board and the bottom righthand corner of the Smart Inventor Board.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;854&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]11. Get comfortable with the CoDrone remote! We included a picture for reference.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;855&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215974e87c\" name=\"6a2215974e87c\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Remote Control<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>Still not sure where all of the wires go? We have a beautiful photograph for you!<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;856&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 6 Build video [vc_column_text] If you'd like to see the full-length build video with more detail, you can check that out\u00a0here. [\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=mDDdWtQXyF4&amp;feature=emb_logo\" align=\"center\"] [\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column] Step 7 The&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-arduino-build-the-remote\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1752,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":804,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[2168,2164,2165,2177,2111],"class_list":["post-844","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-build","lesson-tag-codrone","lesson-tag-codrone-pro","lesson-tag-getting-started","lesson-tag-remote-control","module-getting-started","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/844","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":1,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/844\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":857,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/844\/revisions\/857"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1752"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=844"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=844"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=844"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}